{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410694-do-you-typically-play-childlings-wilders-or-grumps","id":1410694,"title":"Do you typically play childlings, wilders or grumps?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-27T09:24:09-07:00","id":1410694,"title":"Do you typically play childlings, wilders or grumps?","content":"I usually play wilders, but I\u2019ve played other ages too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:40:13-07:00","id":1410706,"title":"","content":"Grumps have really come into theirown in c20. Before they were basically &quot;your last leg&quot;(Unless you were a troll then it was &quot;play this&quot;). Now they can work out pretty solidly as the &quot;responsible adult&quot; for your group being able to handle all the mundane stuff while being pulled around by childlings and wilders to cancel what little banality gets through.. its a pretty neat symbiosis. I imagine now many more rulers are Grumps than 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:57:49-07:00","id":1410711,"title":"","content":"Pre-C20, everyone I knew tended to play Wilders 95% of the time. Childlings having to be literal children, and the game eventually turning you into a Grump anyway made it the only real functional choice.<br /> <br /> In C20, I've seen more variety, though oddly a lot of people flocking to Grump now that being the old folks of Seemings is a lot more fun. Personally though, Childlings are currently winning in my play experience (probably because I can play a bunch of neat ideas from the old days but with PCs in their early 20s or so making them way less squicky) ever so slightly (3 to 1 to 1)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T17:10:37-07:00","id":1410785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1410694-do-you-typically-play-childlings-wilders-or-grumps?p=1410711#post1410711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-C20, everyone I knew tended to play Wilders 95% of the time. Childlings having to be literal children, and the game eventually turning you into a Grump anyway made it the only real functional choice.<br /> <br /> In C20, I've seen more variety, though oddly a lot of people flocking to Grump now that being the old folks of Seemings is a lot more fun. Personally though, Childlings are currently winning in my play experience (probably because I can play a bunch of neat ideas from the old days but with PCs in their early 20s or so making them way less squicky) ever so slightly (3 to 1 to 1)</div> </div> </div> </div>Every motley needs a responsible adult \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T17:32:29-07:00","id":1410789,"title":"","content":"It's been a while since I've played. But I'd probably tend to play Grumps nowadays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T19:10:19-07:00","id":1410793,"title":"","content":"Thanks to the way the rules where set up, Grumps where Banality infested geezers that would get undone way to early and Childings where literally children, and small children can\u2019t get up to most adventures or intrigue plots.<br /> <br /> So yeah most people picked Wildres because they where the only seeming that could do crud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T23:18:51-07:00","id":1410806,"title":"","content":"Mostly Grumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T01:08:44-07:00","id":1410811,"title":"","content":"Grumps and Wilders, especially before they unsynchronized them to age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T04:23:14-07:00","id":1410824,"title":"","content":"I guess I identify most with the Wilder. Too \u201csophisticated\u201d to be a Childling, not \u201cresponsible\u201d enough to settle down and be a Grump lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}